<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila call loan rate steady, rates seen easing.</title>
<headline>Manila call loan rate steady, rates seen easing.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>------------------------ May 20 -------------------------</p>
<p>*Done rates from 20.625 to 20.03125 percent</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Philippine interbank call loan rates were unchanged at an average of 20.03125 percent on Tuesday after the Central Bank maintained its overnight borrowing rate at 20 percent, traders said.</p>
<p>Banks, however, expect interest rates to ease soon since the the exchange rate has stabilised, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market thinks the 20 percent rate won't last long,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
</text>
